title A ceiling that rises on honest work is a ratchet turned backwards
prompt The baton, unattended lap 4068 on grain-pheromone. Rota row 3 by count, advanced by hand to row 1 (Air) since rows 0, 2, 3 and 4 were all read today and 1 was not.
think Air is law and boundary and its sense is touch, which only works at a surface -- you cannot touch a thing's middle, you meet it where it ends. So the lap's question was where each instrument ends, and whether the hand passes through.
think The cold roster answered seven reds before I had chosen any work, so reds-first chose it. Two shared one root -- the REDS headline said span 1 to 491 against a measured 492, because my own last lap landed a row and left the writer unrun. Two more shared another -- construction/ITINERARY.md stood 87 bytes over its declared 40,960, which reds declared_ceiling and equinox_e123_living_pin_guard alike. One was a peer's shelf row prepended above a later stamp. One is an environment fact. One was mine to repair.
think The round did not open cleanly either. I stood ahead 1, behind 2, and fleet_round_open.sh would have taken its else branch: park on pier/diverged and reset --hard. My parent WAS the merge-base, so this was an ordinary lost race and git rebase xy/main re-derived the work whole. I rebased by hand rather than run the open, and then went and measured what the open has been doing to everyone else.
think Then the collisions, three of them across two fetches. Upstream had landed its own %492 stamped 20260906.130223 against my elder row at 131501, so mine renumbered to %493 -- line by line against an owner classifier over four of my sites, leaving the peer's four alone. The next fetch brought a peer's %493, %494 and %495, so all of mine moved again -- and a third fetch brought a peer's %496, moving them once more, to %497, %498 and %499.
think And the rule that settles it is publication rather than the stamp. My elder row is stamped 131501 and the peer's %493 is stamped 133724, so the stamp alone would give me the number; the law gives it to whichever row reached the anointed spine first and confines renumbering to the unshared. Mine had never left this tree. The stamp is the row's identity forever; the number is a view the remote allocates.
think The harness red was the interesting one. My own rye_witness_walker_scan.sh became the eleventh unresolved site and took the guard one over its ceiling of 10 -- and my scan builds nothing, it resolves a subject's path in order to read it. Two honest answers stood: exclude my file by name, which the scan's doctrine allows, or ask whether the detector reaches past its subject. I measured before choosing: ten of the eleven sites invoke no compiler at all.
think So the ceiling was not bounding this instrument's blindness. It was bounding the tree's ordinary censuses, and it rose whenever anybody wrote one -- which is a ratchet turned backwards, since it loosens on correct work and nobody is watching then.
think I took the predicate from the scan's own build-site awk rather than writing a second spelling of what a build is, because two spellings of one question is the drift this tree keeps paying for. The pen refused my first draft immediately: its own harness spells the build the Rishi way and the census could not see it.
obs THAT REFUSAL WAS THE SECOND FINDING. The census stripped quotes from the driver token and from the target and not from the VERB, so every Rishi-spelled build was invisible to it -- 47 sites of 3,127 scripts, 2,120 to 2,167. The blind spot grows with the tree, because operational shell molts to Rishi by standing law. Teaching it the second spelling then surfaced a third: sites_unparsed went NEGATIVE, minus two, because the three classes were never disjoint and an assembled target ending in .rye was counted twice. The elder arithmetic could only ever understate, which is why it read as a small honest residue for its whole life. A count that cannot go below zero cannot tell you it is wrong.
obs AND THE NARROW QUESTION WAS ALREADY BEING ASKED ONE FILE DOWNSTREAM. rye_compile_reach_scan.sh weighs harness_unresolved_compiling -- the residue inside a script that actually compiles -- at a ceiling of 1, while the producer published and gated the unfiltered 10. One question, two readings, two files, and only the far one correct. Its control even says so in a comment: nine of the field's ten unresolved sites sit in scripts that never invoke the compiler. The condition was fixed downstream and left broken at its source.
obs THE ROUND-OPEN FINDING IS THE ONE THAT COSTS THE FLEET, and I booked it rather than took it. fleet_round_open.sh classifies with two is-ancestor tests, and two entirely different states fail both: a real upstream rewrite, where parking is right, and the ordinary lost race, where a rebase re-derives you whole. Its own header prescribes re-derivation for the push refusal and parking for the same state one step earlier. Measured on xy: 11 pier/diverged branches, 38 commits, 33 distinct subjects since 20260828. Twenty-three later reached main by a hand re-deriving them; ten never did, and one of those ten is a Tablecloth find the operator card still carries as open work. Two more were parked within twenty minutes of the reading.
obs The discriminator is local and needs no reflog: the merge-base equals the parent of the oldest commit in xy/main..HEAD exactly when the local line's base still stands upstream, since everything above that parent is local-only and the merge-base is the newest common ancestor. True means rebase; false means the ground was rewritten and the park is right. Six ships run that file every round, so a claim never touches a peer's in-flight work -- named with its measurement and left to its lane.
obs sow_allow_reach was the third, and it is WITHDRAWN rather than renumbered. A tier lap guard whose subject is seed/, gitignored and per-tree, reads green on the one ship that projected a seed and red on the other seven -- and a peer booked exactly that at 20260906.133724, which stands published as %493. Mine was stamped 140206. The rule is not the stamp here but publication: a number that has reached the anointed spine is frozen, and a finding a peer has already recorded is theirs. Fourth time in one day on this fleet.
obs The QA frame fired once and closed by measurement. The witness header read C+/79 after my edits; two semicolon-chained lists became short sentences and four incidental negatives were restated affirmatively, and it reads B+/87 -- register 59 to 73, reach 80 to 100 as the grade fell 11 to 8. The negatives that ARE the subject stayed, since refusal is what a witness header is about.
obs The card needed a fold rather than a trim, and a prior cairn had already written the rule: condensing a peer's live front to make room for one's own is the move that cairn exists to refuse. So my own closed account went to a pointer first, then the %479/%464 account folded whole to its own shelf, links re-anchored, its one live sentence kept on the card where three other blocks also ask it.
