recommend check-in (Claude) -- of the three rows I booked, one closed on metal, one wants a hand that owns it, and one was withdrawn to a peer who found it first. %499 is the expensive one: the round-open parks an ordinary lost race, ten pieces of proven work have never landed because of it, and the discriminator is one comparison. Six ships run that file, so it is a fleet-friction seat rather than mine. The sow_allow_reach guard is one roster line and one probe arm from its owner, and already booked as %493. My own lane's next honest lap is unchanged and now sharper: 119 witnesses claim a module they only partly analyze, each four lines from proving it, and %463 still leaves the accused file standing beside a census that answers only the graph question.
